INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(33,79224,31,'The bill celebrating the life of Leon Foster Pope was introduced and quickly moved through the legislative process. It was engrossed and agreed to by the Senate in a smooth progression. The bill passed without any noted opposition.','y','2026-01-09 11:01:51','2026-01-09 11:01:51');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(35,78269,31,'The bill establishing the right to obtain contraception was initially passed by the Senate with a narrow vote of 21-18 and later passed by the House with a substitute by a vote of 54-41. After both chambers agreed on the House\'s substitute, the bill was enrolled and sent to the governor, who proposed amendments. The Senate rejected the governor\'s recommendations, and the bill was communicated back to the governor for final action.','y','2026-01-09 11:01:58','2026-01-09 11:01:58');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(37,77557,31,'The bill regarding land development and solar canopies in surface parking areas was introduced and passed by the House with a vote of 64-32. It then moved to the Senate, where it passed with amendments by a narrow vote of 21-18. However, after being sent to the Governor, the bill was vetoed, and the House subsequently sustained the Governor\'s veto, preventing it from becoming law.','y','2026-01-09 11:02:02','2026-01-09 11:02:02');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(40,76912,31,'The bill, which aimed to develop and administer Standards of Learning assessments in languages other than English, was introduced and referred to the Committee on Education and Health. After being reported from this committee with a substitute, it was sent to the Finance and Appropriations Committee. However, the bill did not advance further as it was left in the Finance and Appropriations Committee without a vote, effectively halting its progress.','y','2026-01-09 11:02:10','2026-01-09 11:02:10');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(58,79529,31,'The bill commending J. Dean Norton was introduced and quickly moved through the legislative process. It was engrossed by the Senate and agreed to by a voice vote, indicating no significant opposition. The legislation successfully passed in the Senate.','y','2026-01-09 13:15:04','2026-01-09 13:15:04');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(49,78258,31,'The bill, which amends the definition of \"psychiatric emergency department\" for involuntary temporary detention orders, was introduced by a Republican and successfully passed through both the Senate and the House with unanimous votes. It was then signed by the Speaker and the President before being communicated to the Governor. The Governor approved the bill, and it became law, effective July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:15','2026-01-09 12:02:15');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(41,77733,31,'The bill aimed to establish a functional literacy program for inmates and successfully passed through both the House and Senate with amendments, receiving near-unanimous support in the Senate and strong support in the House. After a conference committee resolved differences between the two chambers, the final version was agreed upon by both the House and Senate. However, the governor returned the bill with recommendations, and the House narrowly voted to delay action on these recommendations, which were communicated back to the governor for further consideration.','y','2026-01-09 12:01:54','2026-01-09 12:01:54');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(43,78556,31,'The bill aimed at amending the charter and powers of the city council of Poquoson was introduced and referred to the Committee on Counties, Cities and Towns. It was assigned to a subcommittee and placed on the committee\'s agenda but was ultimately left in the committee without a vote. This effectively ended the bill\'s progress, preventing it from advancing to the full House for consideration.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:00','2026-01-09 12:02:00');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(44,78552,31,'The bill, which aimed to develop a model policy for school bathroom safety checks, was introduced and referred to the Committee on Education. Despite receiving a fiscal impact statement, the bill did not advance past the committee stage and was left in the Education Committee, effectively halting its progress.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:02','2026-01-09 12:02:02');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(42,76706,31,'The bill proposing a constitutional amendment to establish a fundamental right to reproductive freedom was initially continued to 2025 by the House Privileges and Elections Committee. It was later reported with a substitute and narrowly passed the House with a 51-48 vote. The Senate also agreed to the bill with a 21-18 vote, and it was subsequently enrolled, signed by legislative leaders, and assigned as Chapter 600, set to take effect on July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 12:01:57','2026-01-09 12:01:57');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(45,77462,31,'The bill addressing unlawful discriminatory housing practices was introduced and referred to the Committee on General Laws, where it was assigned to a subcommittee on Housing/Consumer Protection. Despite being placed on the agenda twice, it did not advance and was ultimately left in the General Laws committee. As a result, the bill did not progress further in the legislative process and did not become law.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:05','2026-01-09 12:02:05');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(46,76741,31,'The bill permitting sports betting on Virginia college sports was introduced and referred to the Committee on General Laws and Technology, where it was reported favorably with a near-unanimous vote. It was then sent to the Finance and Appropriations Committee, where it was continued to 2025 with unanimous support. Ultimately, the bill was left in the Finance and Appropriations Committee and did not advance further.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:07','2026-01-09 12:02:07');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(48,79465,31,'The bill celebrating the life of William Gerald Massengill was introduced and presented in the Senate. It was quickly engrossed and agreed to by the Senate on the same day. The bill passed without any recorded opposition, indicating unanimous or near-unanimous support.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:10','2026-01-09 12:02:10');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(47,77771,31,'The bill aimed at repealing the four-level classification system for enhanced earned sentence credits was introduced by a Republican and referred to the Committee on Rules. It did not advance further as it was left in the Rules committee without a vote, effectively killing the legislation.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:09','2026-01-09 12:02:09');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(50,79881,31,'The bill commending Leland C. Teets was introduced and presented in the Senate. It was laid on the Clerk\'s Desk and subsequently engrossed by the Senate. The Senate agreed to the bill by a voice vote, and it passed without any recorded opposition.','y','2026-01-09 12:02:18','2026-01-09 12:02:18');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(59,78115,31,'The bill, which allows counties, cities, and towns to include tiny homes or accessory dwelling units in their comprehensive plans, passed the House unanimously and the Senate with a near-unanimous vote. After the Senate made a substitute amendment, the House agreed to it without opposition. The governor approved the bill, and it became law, effective July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 13:15:06','2026-01-09 13:15:06');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(51,77302,31,'The bill, concerning tenant remedies under the Virginia Residential Landlord and Tenant Act, passed the House with a narrow majority and then the Senate with a similarly close vote. After being signed by the Speaker and President, it was sent to the Governor, who vetoed it. The House ultimately sustained the Governor\'s veto, preventing the bill from becoming law.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:48','2026-01-09 13:14:48');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(53,77668,31,'The bill regarding health insurance carrier business practices was introduced and unanimously passed through the House after being reported with a substitute from the Labor and Commerce Committee. It then moved to the Senate, where it was also unanimously approved after being reported from the Commerce and Labor Committee. The bill was subsequently signed by both the Speaker and the President, communicated to the Governor, and approved, becoming law effective July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:51','2026-01-09 13:14:51');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(52,78892,31,'The bill concerning data centers and local authority on land use applications was introduced and referred to the Committee on Counties, Cities and Towns. It was assigned to a subcommittee and placed on the committee\'s agenda. However, the bill did not advance further and was left in the committee, effectively halting its progress.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:50','2026-01-09 13:14:50');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(54,79024,31,'The bill, which aimed to amend the six-year capital outlay plan and funding requirements, was introduced in the Senate and passed unanimously through the Finance and Appropriations Committee and the full Senate. It then moved to the House, where it also passed unanimously. The governor approved the bill, and it became law, effective July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:53','2026-01-09 13:14:53');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(55,78235,31,'The bill aimed at enhancing earned sentence credits was introduced by a Republican and referred to the Committee on Rehabilitation and Social Services. It was ultimately passed by indefinitely in the committee with a narrow vote of 8 in favor and 7 against, effectively halting its progress. This means the bill did not advance further in the legislative process and was not considered by the full Senate or House.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:57','2026-01-09 13:14:57');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(56,79928,31,'The bill commending Tarrallton Elementary School was introduced and laid on the Speaker\'s table, then quickly engrossed and agreed to by the House through a voice vote. It successfully passed the House without any recorded opposition.','y','2026-01-09 13:14:59','2026-01-09 13:14:59');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `bills_status_narratives` VALUES
(57,77053,31,'The bill regarding site assessments for high energy use facilities passed both the Virginia House and Senate after amendments and a conference committee, but faced challenges with the governor. The governor made recommendations, which the House rejected by a wide margin. Ultimately, the motion to pass the bill in its enrolled form was also rejected, leaving its future uncertain.','y','2026-01-09 13:15:02','2026-01-09 13:15:02');
