(16260,5059,76706,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.17.78.28','That was a bug, Will—thanks for pointing it out. (The General Assembly has made some really great changes to their website, but they\'re a bear to adapt to, in a technical sense.)','comment','published','n','2025-01-09 03:17:34','2025-01-09 03:17:34');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `comments` VALUES
(16101,90324,74071,'Cindy','example@example.com',NULL,'127.116.167.167','Getting rid of the Robert E. Lee License Plate is not going to get rid of Robert E. Lee\'s history or memory, all it does is infringe upon my Constitutional 1st Amendments Rights.  I am one of the approximately 2000 people who have this plate, and have used it for several years. NOT ONE SINGLE TIME have I ever received a negative comment about it, not so much as a dirty look or a middle finger, from anybody of any race.  I\'ve actually had positive comments from members of the Black community about that plate. There\'s not a whole lot of people who can say, with any honesty, that they actually pay attention to the license plate on any vehicle, unless they\'re needing that number to report an accident or a crime. \nInstead of trying to erase my history, why not do something to teach and promote their own history?  There are plenty of prominent and important Virginia Blacks who could be honored; how about Booker T. Washington, or Mary Smith Kelsey Peake, Matilda Sissieretta Joyner Jones, John Mitchell Jr., John Dabney, Robert Russa Moton, Virginia Randolph, Maggie L. Walker, Bessie Griffin, Aiken C. Taylor, William Harvey Carney, Barbara Johns, Vernon Johns, Oliver White Hill, Donald R. Lyons, Emanuel Logan, George Edward Alcorn, Henry L. Marsh III, and L. Douglas Wilder.  There are hundreds of Black people from this state that deserve recognition, and I\'m willing to bet that the writer and supporters of this bill have no clue who any of these people are or what they did, with the exception of the first and last ones. Any one of them would be a whole lot better than the radical black power fist they chose to put on a license plate.  With all the wonderful, brilliant, and amazing people they should be honoring, they purposely choose to ignore and forget them, virtually erasing them from history, to further promote hatred and division.','comment','published','n','2024-01-20 20:16:55','2024-01-20 20:16:55'),
(16102,5059,74071,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.109.95.176','The fact that you see license plates honoring Black Americans as the opposite of license plates honoring Robert E. Lee is <em>amazing.</em> You just gave away the whole game.\n\nNobody has a constitutional right to have a state-issued license plate with any particular art. No law is stopping you from putting a bumper sticker on your car that says \"racist,\" which would accomplish the same thing as a Robert E. Lee plate. You have as much of a first amendment right to a DMV-produced Robert E. Lee plate as a Nazi does to a DMV-produced Adolf Hitler license plate—which is to say, none.','comment','published','n','2024-01-20 20:29:46','2024-01-20 20:29:46'),
(16234,90876,74071,'Nancy Arker','example@example.com',NULL,'127.186.250.183','I am ordering this license plate. \nAnd I will keep it on my car I don’t care who pulls me over.\nIt will stay I swear on my blood as a Virginian Man who is related to confederate soilders.\nThis is communism. Leave our history alone.\nThe communists and their thug horde have destroyed our monuments, is that not enough?\nI saw the domestic terrorism in Richmond when the BLM riots happened. It was disgusting, filthy and it should have never EVER been allowed to happen the way it did. \nCan we not even have a simple license plate?\nWake up Virginia! They will stop at nothing to erase OUR history, OUR culture and OUR heritage.','comment','published','n','2024-03-26 01:18:15','2024-03-26 01:18:15'),
(16235,5059,74071,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.236.146.1','Nancy Arker, \"a Virginia Man,\" thinks that it\'s \"communism\" not to be able to have a Robert E. Lee license plate. Mr. Arker contains multitudes!','comment','published','n','2024-03-26 02:23:44','2024-03-26 02:23:44');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `comments` VALUES
(16107,90257,74585,'Michael A','example@example.com',NULL,'127.17.20.119','If this bill become law, it will guarantee greater expenditure for undefined improvements in ESL results. Establishment of ratios appears at first blush to be a scientific measure. In reality, it is a sliding scale susceptible to pressure from unions to add addition staff. Please withdraw it.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 15:05:47','2024-01-21 15:05:47'),
(16108,90281,74585,'Lou Di Leonardo','example@example.com',NULL,'127.147.54.137','This is a teachers\' union dream where they can get more teachers hired if kids don\'t or won\'t learn proper English.  Foreign language students should be mainstreamed, i.e. put into the same classes with others so that they will learn the English language sooner and better.  American kids who can\'t/won\'t speak English properly should be kept after school for remedial instruction so that they don\'t hold back the children who do want to learn to speak properly.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 15:26:36','2024-01-21 15:26:36'),
(16109,90325,74585,'Bill Denk','example@example.com',NULL,'127.205.245.93','It appears that this Bill  HB 1247 is a mandate to decrease the rate of English language learning. It requires a dramatic increase in the number of teachers of ESL and incentivises teachers to NOT promote students to the next level but to rather score them at low proficiency levels to increase and maximize teacher staffing. I did not see any analysis of what would be the cost of this mandate to the State as well local school boards.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 16:02:03','2024-01-21 16:02:03'),
(16110,90262,74585,'Bill Peabody','example@example.com',NULL,'127.183.246.211','How much did we spend on the waves of Eastern europeans,germans and Italians when they came out over before WW1?\n$0?','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 16:18:24','2024-01-21 16:18:24'),
(16117,90330,74585,'Lou Di Leonardo','example@example.com',NULL,'127.171.212.76','And after WW2?  Zero.  What changed?','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 21:55:50','2024-01-21 21:55:50'),
(16118,5059,74585,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.11.1.124','Y\'all just made up a non-existent thing to be angry about. You don\'t think that schools had to teach kids English until, like, 1990 or whatever? ...How the heck do you think they learned the language when coming here from Germany, Italy, Austria, Hungary, France, and Greece? They didn\'t just arrive, show up for 5th grade the next day and start speaking English—schools bore the costs of ensuring that those kids learned English. The same as now.','comment','published','n','2024-01-22 00:24:53','2024-01-22 00:24:53'),
(16119,90299,74585,'Will Weaver','example@example.com',NULL,'127.56.47.167','Some of these comments really make my head hurt. The ignorance is staggering.','comment','published','n','2024-01-22 13:44:45','2024-01-22 13:44:45'),
(16136,90384,74585,'Charles McAndrew','example@example.com',NULL,'127.23.213.164','I vote NO for this bill!','comment','published','n','2024-01-25 01:11:33','2024-01-25 01:11:33'),
(16138,90391,74585,'Lou Di Leonardo','example@example.com',NULL,'127.151.62.244','It appears some of the outraged commenters with headaches don\'t have their facts straight, just their feelings.  Schools did NOT have special programs to teach English to new arrivals from Europe or anywhere else (China, for example).  Kids learned by watching TV, playing with other kids, and, if old enough, by going to night school for instruction. They learned because they wanted to learn.  Today, even with English taught to native (that means born here, like me) Americans many in some cities speak an unintelligible version that needs subtitles when spoken on TV.  If kids are babied, they stay babies.  If they want to learn, they will.  Money isn\'t the answer, a willing spirit is.','comment','published','n','2024-01-25 16:08:47','2024-01-25 16:08:47'),
(16139,5059,74585,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.81.243.171','I\'m afraid that you\'ve been given a false version of history. The 1924 Supreme Court decision <em><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meyer_v._Nebraska\">Meyer v. Nebraska</a></em> held that it was illegal for states to require English-only instruction under \"sink-or-swim\" policies that were put into place during World War I because of anti-German sentiment.\r\n\r\nBut, also, the \"sink-or-swim\" approach didn\'t work! People just didn\'t learn English, or learned it badly, which made it difficult for them to assimilate. For example, there were areas of the country where people spoke only German well into the 20th century, as Wilkerson & Salmons documented in their 2008 paper, \"<a href=\"https://watermark.silverchair.com/ASp83.3.1Wilkerson-Salmons.pdf?token=AQECAHi208BE49Ooan9kkhW_Ercy7Dm3ZL_9Cf3qfKAc485ysgAAA4QwggOABgkqhkiG9w0BBwagggNxMIIDbQIBADCCA2YGCSqGSIb3DQEHATAeBglghkgBZQMEAS4wEQQMLY3qvVIP8HC6TOY_AgEQgIIDNzSzS4SuktcIVNsKlj3jM2DDs1q4zVS8XuCciSsBLhcaHfYLcdeqaSpq0ToVtGEB15FShYQWboYdw6QMADv711oauXD-x_IzEVFZE-KW0YPse_ZYa_6hc6VUlY4LakhiDWLc47RPDCe2a8oAy3sPflGqnqILLO5kSZ7jLyyNfcinlt-Q9sbQQj66jQjUptmIioypIrIvptEI8ZHJEMFz3UCoD7wKZ166UlrOvI5VY0huJWtcVniJ21o3yqj4RiA-vo-GVF_Abl1ub7eB4TZ5Fk8Ss1UhzZWsc7AWjWfvLP7D4tjwHfE3RDAelIeCmgw609K90Yv9PJa8uFlwH3MRe20rfqc9qDIFStRBQyzvlruNpbdcvP_eOM574cDbf1kzqUm5a16c6lKQz_JwLXfZihaUFuAQjbMuuNpuLzdeMp0pqOWMWCMGcgTP-MZYDW68CebEXRRlorcdLkqvw4682NmECNSEAOM_nMjS4mIYiWfzTPYwd2eProVm2keWUhAC-Oi_6WENeDJNHuW5jkCyhJKrCcgEP4B9UW63200cqp7TXzl03m8gO6WjaYZ2iSMNHseEWuoq8P5QS-n_BKwFMk5jbDhl7ziguQE5TU0a9rZHupsyHK6e6-nVR_--aTA0nWpcCvNmvaPtq1-G-wf2qX7LE7VvOLUlpsLUO2WRVBH3ODd8YXxgxXL5-SIfkRY5Bq1Xbjzc7OQndCQqgSsFPOBu88TIw5Ly-mIgx5tswEgIHT2G-wU4wTDNlCua4bWQyXmeFl0V-KU62s4bV7yZmbtfLaQ-2z-A2C_l8kDecO8fd9reefLLy9E2Jic7ioCHVnWcg0CBHxsA08sVXul9wnQZaqKTGu6d9yyVR8kRYyF0wsoP7X_JUbBEXnu9shZcasqD1jwXwbu29jV1DQI-aIpGFgxOh62YA0AS53ZLofQJ6qXbMEf0d8OAADuhjSsqDefwxGZCSy50FEpMD2BK4mTq-cRJA6yh-WFfVWednuYn1MEkKDSy1vDswXfK-y1kT4a8ePKJ7JEPoME43Nb9fTBoKvNeijqCaZNdt1K7RqN9Lvq7S9LbpqxccVg1vQTJdKT0Wi4Pjck\">“Good Old Immigrants of Yesteryear” Who Didn\'t Learn English:\r\nGermans in Wisconsin</a>.\" That\'s part of a considerable body of scholarship that finds that there was no golden age where people just spontaneously learned English. That paper is full of quotations and relevant references.','comment','published','n','2024-01-25 17:32:45','2024-01-25 17:32:45'),
(16238,90919,74585,'Amanda M.','example@example.com',NULL,'127.246.152.103','The levels aren\'t scored locally. In Virginia they use the WIDA ACCESS test, scored by DATA Recognition Corporation for grades 1st-12th.\n\n\nEnglish as a Second Language (ESL) public education in the United States has a relatively recent history, evolving largely in response to waves of immigration and the increasing need for English proficiency among non-native speakers. Here\'s a brief overview:\n\nThe Immigration Act of 1965 led to a significant increase in immigration from non-European countries, further emphasizing the need for structured ESL programs in public schools.\nBilingual Education and the Lau v. Nichols Decision (1974):\nThe Lau v. Nichols Supreme Court decision in 1974 mandated that schools must provide equal educational opportunities to students who do not speak English as their primary language. This led to the development of bilingual education programs across the country. Bilingual education programs aimed to provide academic instruction in both English and the student\'s native language, with the goal of transitioning students to English proficiency.\nShift to English Immersion and ESL Programs (Late 20th Century):\nIn the 1980s and 1990s, there was a shift away from bilingual education towards English immersion programs and ESL instruction.\nEnglish as a Second Language (ESL) programs became more common, focusing on intensive English language instruction to help students acquire English proficiency more quickly.\nNo Child Left Behind Act and Accountability (2001):\nThe No Child Left Behind Act of 2001 emphasized accountability for English language learners (ELLs) and mandated standardized testing in English proficiency. Schools were required to demonstrate progress in English language acquisition among ELL students, leading to increased attention to ESL programs and teacher training.\n21st Century:\nThroughout the 21st century, ESL education continued to evolve with a focus on research-based instructional practices, cultural sensitivity, and support for diverse student populations.\nMany schools offer ESL programs ranging from pull-out instruction to full-time immersion, depending on the needs of the students and the resources available.\nOverall, the history of ESL public education in the United States reflects the country\'s commitment to providing opportunities for non-native English speakers to acquire proficiency in the language and succeed academically and socially.\n\nI am very confused about comments saying students used to learn English from television. Also, ESL programs do not focus long on basic interpersonal communications skills but rather academic language proficiency. Students test out of ESL.','comment','published','n','2024-04-23 16:46:51','2024-04-23 16:46:51');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `comments` VALUES
(16204,90550,74875,'Yvonne Williams','example@example.com',NULL,'127.39.61.47','Vote NO on senate bill 567','comment','published','n','2024-02-09 01:28:08','2024-02-09 01:28:08'),
(16205,90551,74875,'Dawn Aucoin','example@example.com',NULL,'127.45.243.143','I oppose SB567 and encourage you to vote NO! Decisions about Industrial Commercial Solar Farms need to be kept at the local level. Solar companies are trying to site in Residential, Planning Areas, Wetlands and Conservation areas. Without any regards to areas set aside for them in our county, Prince George County. The SCC will not be able to know about our counties like we do.','comment','published','n','2024-02-09 01:34:42','2024-02-09 01:34:42'),
(16206,90552,74875,'Michelle Coker','example@example.com',NULL,'127.186.65.19','I oppose SB567 and encourage you to vote NO! Consider a solar farm surrounding your home and land completly. Decisions about Industrial Commercial Solar Farms need to be kept at the local level where residents should have a say. Solar companies are trying to site in Residential, Planning Areas, Wetlands and Conservation areas without any regards to area set aside for them in our county. The SCC will not be able to know about our counties planning and policys like we do. Prince George County has turned down such a site at this time because big solar companies want to come in and take over.','comment','published','n','2024-02-09 01:46:12','2024-02-09 01:46:12');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `comments` VALUES
(16105,90320,74452,'Bill Peabody','example@example.com',NULL,'127.119.123.54','Avoid the \"harm\" of a 180lb male crashing into a 135lb female.\nVote yes','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 12:06:57','2024-01-21 12:06:57'),
(16114,5059,74452,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.110.90.236','Maybe it\'s just me, but I think it\'s weird and wrong to refuse to let kids play high school sports because they\'re too small or large compared to the average participant.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 19:50:50','2024-01-21 19:50:50'),
(16185,90512,74452,'Mary Keleher','example@example.com',NULL,'127.18.50.107','Waldo Jaquith, You don\'t think it\'s weird or wrong then men are now being crowned champions in women\'s sports? This bill isn\'t preventing any child from playing sports. This bill is to prevent biological males from competing in women\'s sports. Boys and men can still compete on boy\'s teams and men\'s teams.','comment','published','n','2024-02-05 20:55:53','2024-02-05 20:55:53'),
(16186,5059,74452,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.188.189.212','Yeah, this is not a real problem. You might as well complain that golden retrievers keep winning basketball tournaments because you once watched <em>Air Bud.</em> There are no \"men being crowned champions in women\'s sports\" in Virginia. Not one. This is legislation about a thing that isn\'t a real problem that has been whipped up by far-right creeps in order to make you angry. There is absolutely no definition of \"biological males\" that can pass muster. It doesn\'t exist. Will we exclude boys who have gynecomastia? Girls with elevated testosterone levels? Boys with Klinefelter syndrome? Boys with elevated estrogen levels? Girls with oversized clitorises? Don\'t you think it is extremely gross and bad that you and I are discussing the size of children\'s genitalia?\r\n\r\nThis bill would allow absolutely anybody to challenge the gender of any child playing sports. Do you know how offensive and damaging that is to a child? For an adult to declare \"you are not a real girl,\" and then the girl has to have her genitals examined by a doctor to prove to the creepy parent that they really are a girl? What if that\'s how the girl discovers that she\'s one of the millions of Americans who lie between sexes? Is anybody who isn\'t 100% girl (whatever that even <em>means</em>) automatically a boy?\r\n\r\nOne thing I like to do is <em>not think about children\'s genitals.</em> There are no boys out there pretending to be girls so they that can, like, dominate at field hockey or whatever, any more than there are golden retrievers winning basketball tournaments because, hey, there\'s no rule against it. This is a law that requires that teachers pay real close attention to kids\' genitals. Stop paying attention to kids\' genitals. Stop doing that. It\'s super disgusting.','comment','published','n','2024-02-05 21:18:03','2024-02-05 21:18:03'),
(16188,90299,74452,'Will Weaver','example@example.com',NULL,'127.168.111.54','This is yet another creepy anti-trans bill that needs to be defeated just like the others. Waldo does an incredible job of explaining exactly what is problematic with it. Not to mention it erases intersex people like pretty much all the other bills like this do.\n\nAlso, Waldo, golden retrievers winning basketball tournaments is definitely a concern considering the UMBC Retrievers upset #1 UVA back in 2018. ;)','comment','published','n','2024-02-06 14:25:35','2024-02-06 14:25:35'),
(16193,90534,74452,'Donna','example@example.com',NULL,'127.52.38.9','Delores Oates launched her campaign by discriminating against the LGBTQ community in her home county of Warren after she tried to get their books banned and public library closed. So this bill she has introduced isn’t shocking at all.','comment','published','n','2024-02-07 19:47:06','2024-02-07 19:47:06');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `comments` VALUES
(16200,90545,73896,'Michael William Albin','example@example.com',NULL,'127.18.220.11','Stop assisted suicide legislation now!','comment','published','n','2024-02-08 20:28:17','2024-02-08 20:28:17'),
(16209,90578,73896,'Justin West','example@example.com',NULL,'127.197.232.149','As a Virginia resident and sovereign human being, I should be empowered to make my own end-of-life decisions if I am diagnosed with a terminal illness. I want to be alert, independent, and able to spend time with my loved ones in my final days. \n\nThat is what SB280 would provide. \n\nMore than 70 million Americans in ten states and Washington D.C. already have access to Death with Dignity. As Congresswoman Jennifer Wexton wrote to the committee, “If this bill becomes law in Virginia, it would return the control over to [patients] when, where, and how our stories end, not to the diseases. And that’s the greatest gift you, our elected representatives, can give us.”\n\nDeath with dignity is scandalous to some, including fellow commenter Mr. Albin. It\'s curious how the people dying demented and hopeless, connected to half a dozen tubes in ICU rooms, aren’t considered scandals by anybody. That’s just \"the natural way of things\".\n\n<strong>\"If I cannot give consent to my own death, whose body is this? Who owns my life?\" - Sue Rodriguez <strong>','comment','deleted','n','2024-02-11 01:31:59','2024-02-11 01:31:59');
