INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(40753,73118,'F161',NULL,'<p>According to the 2024 <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+SB61F161+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a> for SB 61, the legislation would have the following negative General Fund revenue impact:\n- $8.1 million in FY 2025\n- $8.1 million in FY 2026\n- $9.4 million in FY 2027\n- $9.5 million in FY 2028\n- $9.6 million in FY 2029\n- $9.7 million in FY 2030\n\nOverall, the total cost over the mentioned fiscal years would be approximately $54.4 million.</p>\n        <p class=\"openai\">Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(41897,74670,'FH1122',NULL,'<p>According to the Fiscal Impact Statement, this legislation is estimated to have a minimal fiscal impact. There would be costs associated with the Board of Medicine and the Board of Nursing to promulgate regulations, but these costs can be handled within existing resources. No specific agency or political subdivisions are mentioned as being affected by this legislation.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(41404,73984,'F122',NULL,'<p>The <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+HB745F122+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a> states that the cost of implementing this legislation, particularly related to the establishment of the Mattress Stewardship Program, would be indeterminate. However, there are specific cost estimates provided for certain aspects of the program:\n\n1. A $50,000 annual cost for an agency-designated external auditor.\n2. Anticipation that additional funds may be required for other aspects beyond plan review.\n3. An estimated negligible revenue increase of $3,350 from additional renovator permits and an increase in revenue of $8,040 from additional sanitizer permits issued by the Virginia Department of Health.\n4. The potential need for additional Compliance Officers to handle increased workload, which could cost approximately $55,000 for a new part-time position.\n\nOverall, while the exact total cost is not specified, the <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+HB745F122+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a> outlines several specific costs and revenue increases that may result from the implementation of this legislation.</p>\n        <p class=\"openai\">Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(40877,73286,'FH2122',NULL,'<p>The Fiscal Impact Statement indicates that the proposed bill, HB267, may have the effect of fewer people being sentenced to jail or prison. However, at this time, there is no available data to estimate the impact on jail or prison bed space needs. The fiscal impact on the Department of Health and Developmental Services and state and local law enforcement agencies is indeterminate and will be updated if additional information is received. Therefore, the specific cost of the legislation is not stated in the statement.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(42222,75107,'FS1122',NULL,'<p>According to the Fiscal Impact Statement, the proposed legislation is not expected to have a state fiscal impact. Adding Fairfax County to the potential casino host locations will not have a fiscal impact on the budget as introduced.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(41864,74616,'FER122',NULL,'<p>This <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+HB1278FH1122+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a> states that there is no fiscal impact associated with this legislation. The Department of Health Professions would not be affected by the provisions of the bill. No specific agency or political subdivisions would be impacted, and no technical amendment is necessary.</p>\n        <p class=\"openai\">Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(41767,74490,'FER122',NULL,'<p>According to the Fiscal Impact Statement, this legislation will cost $160,250 in the fiscal year 2025 and subsequent years. This cost includes salary, benefits, and operating expenses for the Tribal Ombudsman position. The funding will come from the general fund through a budget amendment to the Secretary of the Commonwealth. The other departments and commissions impacted by the bill anticipate that any costs can be absorbed within their current resources.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `fiscal_impact_statements` VALUES
(40680,73030,'F122',NULL,'<p>This Fiscal Impact Statement states that there is no anticipated state fiscal impact resulting from the provisions of this bill. However, the impact to local school divisions is indeterminate.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','2025-01-12 03:10:40','2025-01-12 03:10:40');
